IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-logic`

-- ccc13-securities-title.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part X: sections 382 to 392 (stock exchange manipulation, insider trading, gaming in stocks,
-- brokers, title documents, receipts, trade secrets, disposal of property to defraud creditors).
-- Reading of the answers as in ccc13-fraud.l4. Where a section has a saving, the offence function takes the saving's answer as an input
-- (`the saving applies, by s ...`): JUST TRUE gives JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE leaves the elements to decide, NOTHING is carried.

§ `Part X -- sections 382 to 392`

§§ `Section 382 -- Fraudulent manipulation of stock exchange transactions`

-- src:7194 | Fraudulent manipulation of stock exchange transactions
-- src:7195 | 382 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, through the facility of a stock exchange, curb market or other market, with intent to create a false or misleading appearance of active public trading in a security or with intent to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market price of a security,
-- src:7196 | (a) effects a transaction in the security that involves no change in the beneficial ownership thereof,
-- src:7197 | (b) enters an order for the purchase of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the sale of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons, or
-- src:7198 | (c) enters an order for the sale of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the purchase of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons.
@ref s 382 (src:7194-7198)
GIVEN `the person acts through the facility of a stock exchange, curb market or other market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to create a false or misleading appearance of active public trading in a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market price of a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person effects a transaction in the security that involves no change in the beneficial ownership thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person enters an order for the purchase of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the sale of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person enters an order for the sale of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the purchase of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382 the conduct is the offence of fraudulent manipulation of stock exchange transactions` MEANS
    IF    `the person acts through the facility of a stock exchange, curb market or other market`
      AND (   `the person acts with intent to create a false or misleading appearance of active public trading in a security`
           OR `the person acts with intent to create a false or misleading appearance with respect to the market price of a security`)
      AND (   `the person effects a transaction in the security that involves no change in the beneficial ownership thereof`   -- (a)
           OR `the person enters an order for the purchase of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the sale of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons`   -- (b)
           OR `the person enters an order for the sale of the security, knowing that an order of substantially the same size at substantially the same time and at substantially the same price for the purchase of the security has been or will be entered by or for the same or different persons`)   -- (c)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, through the facility of a stock exchange, curb market or other market"

@ref s 382 (the punishments) (src:7194-7198)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 382 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 382 (the class of the offence) (src:7194-7198)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 382 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§§ `Section 382.1 -- Prohibited insider trading`

-- (4) In this section, inside information means information relating to or affecting the issuer of a security or a security that they have issued, or are about to issue, that (a) has not been generally disclosed; and (b) could reasonably be expected to significantly affect the market price or value of a security of the issuer.
-- src:7212 | Definition of inside information
-- src:7213 | (4) In this section, inside information means information relating to or affecting the issuer of a security or a security that they have issued, or are about to issue, that
-- src:7214 | (a) has not been generally disclosed; and
-- src:7215 | (b) could reasonably be expected to significantly affect the market price or value of a security of the issuer.
@ref s 382.1(4) (src:7212-7215)
GIVEN `the information relates to or affects the issuer of a security or a security that they have issued, or are about to issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information has not been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information could reasonably be expected to significantly affect the market price or value of a security of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382.1(4) the information is inside information` MEANS
    IF    `the information relates to or affects the issuer of a security or a security that they have issued, or are about to issue`
      AND `the information has not been generally disclosed`
      AND `the information could reasonably be expected to significantly affect the market price or value of a security of the issuer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "inside information means information relating to or affecting the issuer of a security"

-- (3) For greater certainty, an act is not an offence under this section if it is authorized or required, or is not prohibited, by any federal or provincial Act or regulation applicable to it.
-- src:7210 | Saving
-- src:7211 | (3) For greater certainty, an act is not an offence under this section if it is authorized or required, or is not prohibited, by any federal or provincial Act or regulation applicable to it.
@ref s 382.1(3) (src:7210-7211)
GIVEN `the act is authorized or required, or is not prohibited, by a federal or provincial Act or regulation applicable to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382.1(3) the act is saved from being an offence under section 382.1` MEANS
    IF `the act is authorized or required, or is not prohibited, by a federal or provincial Act or regulation applicable to it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an act is not an offence under this section if it is authorized or required, or is not prohibited, by any federal or provincial Act or regulation applicable to it"; this subsection gives no saving on these facts

-- (1)(a)-(e): how the inside information came to the person. (e) is information obtained from a person who possesses or obtained it in a manner referred to in (a) to (d).
DECLARE `s 382.1(1) way of coming by the information` IS ONE OF
    `s 382.1(1) possessed by virtue of being a shareholder of the issuer of that security`   -- (a)
    `s 382.1(1) possessed by virtue of, or obtained in the course of, their business or professional relationship with that issuer`   -- (b)
    `s 382.1(1) possessed by virtue of, or obtained in the course of, a proposed takeover or reorganization of, or amalgamation, merger or similar business combination with, that issuer`   -- (c)
    `s 382.1(1) possessed by virtue of, or obtained in the course of, their employment, office, duties or occupation with that issuer or with a person referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c)`   -- (d)
    `s 382.1(1) obtained from a person who possesses or obtained the information in a manner referred to in paragraphs (a) to (d)`   -- (e)
    `s 382.1(1) none of the ways in paragraphs (a) to (e)`

-- src:7199 | Prohibited insider trading
-- src:7200 | 382.1 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, directly or indirectly, buys or sells a security, knowingly using inside information that they
-- src:7201 | (a) possess by virtue of being a shareholder of the issuer of that security;
-- src:7202 | (b) possess by virtue of, or obtained in the course of, their business or professional relationship with that issuer;
-- src:7203 | (c) possess by virtue of, or obtained in the course of, a proposed takeover or reorganization of, or amalgamation, merger or similar business combination with, that issuer;
-- src:7204 | (d) possess by virtue of, or obtained in the course of, their employment, office, duties or occupation with that issuer or with a person referred to in paragraphs (a) to (c); or
-- src:7205 | (e) obtained from a person who possesses or obtained the information in a manner referred to in paragraphs (a) to (d).
@ref s 382.1(1) (src:7199-7205)
GIVEN `the person directly or indirectly buys or sells a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly uses the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is inside information, by s 382.1(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `how the person came by the information` IS A `s 382.1(1) way of coming by the information`
      `the saving applies, by s 382.1(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382.1(1) the conduct is the offence of buying or selling a security using inside information` MEANS
    IF    `the person directly or indirectly buys or sells a security`
      AND `the person knowingly uses the information`
      AND NOT (`how the person came by the information` EQUALS `s 382.1(1) none of the ways in paragraphs (a) to (e)`)
    THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the information is inside information, by s 382.1(4)`, `ccc13 not` `the saving applies, by s 382.1(3)`)
         -- NOTHING passes through from the two inputs; JUST FALSE when the saving applies (the text says the act is not an offence)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, directly or indirectly, buys or sells a security, knowingly using inside information that they"

@ref s 382.1(1) (the punishments) (src:7199-7205)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 382.1(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 382.1(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7199-7205)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 382.1(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2) Except when necessary in the course of business, a person who knowingly conveys inside information that they possess or obtained in a manner referred to in subsection (1) to another person,
-- knowing that there is a risk that the person will use the information to buy or sell ... a security ..., or that they may convey the information to another person who may buy or sell such a security, is guilty of ...
-- "Except when ... met" is decided case by case (the maintainer, 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE once the exception is met, fork F6.
-- src:7206 | Tipping
-- src:7207 | (2) Except when necessary in the course of business, a person who knowingly conveys inside information that they possess or obtained in a manner referred to in subsection (1) to another person, knowing that there is a risk that the person will use the information to buy or sell, directly or indirectly, a security to which the information relates, or that they may convey the information to another person who may buy or sell such a security, is guilty of
-- src:7208 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:7209 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 382.1(2) (src:7206-7209)
GIVEN `the conveying is necessary in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly conveys the information to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is inside information, by s 382.1(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `how the person came by the information` IS A `s 382.1(1) way of coming by the information`
      `the person knows there is a risk that the other person will use the information to buy or sell a security to which it relates, or may convey it to another person who may buy or sell such a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the saving applies, by s 382.1(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 382.1(2) the conduct is the offence of tipping` MEANS
    IF `the conveying is necessary in the course of business`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except when necessary in the course of business"
    ELSE IF    `the person knowingly conveys the information to another person`
           AND NOT (`how the person came by the information` EQUALS `s 382.1(1) none of the ways in paragraphs (a) to (e)`)
           AND `the person knows there is a risk that the other person will use the information to buy or sell a security to which it relates, or may convey it to another person who may buy or sell such a security`
         THEN `ccc13 all of` (LIST `the information is inside information, by s 382.1(4)`, `ccc13 not` `the saving applies, by s 382.1(3)`)
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person who knowingly conveys inside information that they possess or obtained in a manner referred to in subsection (1) to another person"

@ref s 382.1(2) (the punishments) (src:7206-7209)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 382.1(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 382.1(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7206-7209)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 382.1(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§§ `Section 383 -- Gaming in stocks or merchandise`

-- (1) Every person ... who, with intent to make gain or profit by the rise or fall in price of the stock of an incorporated or unincorporated company or undertaking, whether in or outside Canada, or of any goods, wares or merchandise,
-- (a) makes or signs, or authorizes to be made or signed, any contract or agreement ... purporting to be for the purchase or sale of shares of stock or goods, wares or merchandise, without the bona fide intention of acquiring ... or of selling them ...; or
-- (b) ... in respect of which no delivery of the thing sold or purchased is made or received, and without the bona fide intention of making or receiving delivery thereof ...
-- This section does not apply if a broker, on behalf of a purchaser, receives delivery, even if the broker retains or pledges what is delivered as security for the advance of the purchase money or any part of it.
-- src:7216 | Gaming in stocks or merchandise
-- src:7217 | 383 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, with intent to make gain or profit by the rise or fall in price of the stock of an incorporated or unincorporated company or undertaking, whether in or outside Canada, or of any goods, wares or merchandise,
-- src:7218 | (a) makes or signs, or authorizes to be made or signed, any contract or agreement, oral or written, purporting to be for the purchase or sale of shares of stock or goods, wares or merchandise, without the bona fide intention of acquiring the shares, goods, wares or merchandise or of selling them, as the case may be, or
-- src:7219 | (b) makes or signs, or authorizes to be made or signed, any contract or agreement, oral or written, purporting to be for the sale or purchase of shares of stock or goods, wares or merchandise in respect of which no delivery of the thing sold or purchased is made or received, and without the bona fide intention of making or receiving delivery thereof, as the case may be.
-- src:7220 | This section does not apply if a broker, on behalf of a purchaser, receives delivery, even if the broker retains or pledges what is delivered as security for the advance of the purchase money or any part of it.
@ref s 383(1) (src:7216-7220)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to make gain or profit by the rise or fall in price of the stock of a company or undertaking, or of goods, wares or merchandise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is goods, by s 379` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is shares of stock, or wares or merchandise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes or signs, or authorizes to be made or signed, a contract or agreement purporting to be for the purchase or sale of those things` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without the bona fide intention of acquiring or of selling them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no delivery of the thing sold or purchased is made or received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without the bona fide intention of making or receiving delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a broker, on behalf of a purchaser, receives delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 383(1) the conduct is the offence of gaming in stocks or merchandise` MEANS
    IF `a broker, on behalf of a purchaser, receives delivery`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply if a broker, on behalf of a purchaser, receives delivery"
    ELSE IF    `the person acts with intent to make gain or profit by the rise or fall in price of the stock of a company or undertaking, or of goods, wares or merchandise`
           AND `the person makes or signs, or authorizes to be made or signed, a contract or agreement purporting to be for the purchase or sale of those things`
           AND (   `the person acts without the bona fide intention of acquiring or of selling them`   -- (a)
                OR (`no delivery of the thing sold or purchased is made or received` AND `the person acts without the bona fide intention of making or receiving delivery`))   -- (b)
         THEN `ccc13 any of` (LIST `the thing is goods, by s 379`, JUST `the thing is shares of stock, or wares or merchandise`)
              -- JUST FALSE when the thing is none of shares of stock, goods, wares or merchandise: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "purporting to be for the purchase or sale of shares of stock or goods, wares or merchandise"
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, with intent to make gain or profit by the rise or fall in price of the stock"

@ref s 383(1) (the punishments) (src:7216-7219)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 383(1) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 383(1) (the class of the offence) (src:7216-7219)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 383(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2) Where, in proceedings under this section, it is established that the accused made or signed a contract or an agreement ..., or acted, aided or abetted in the making or signing thereof, the burden of proof of a bona fide intention ... lies on the accused.
-- src:7221 | Onus
-- src:7222 | (2) Where, in proceedings under this section, it is established that the accused made or signed a contract or an agreement for the sale or purchase of shares of stock or goods, wares or merchandise, or acted, aided or abetted in the making or signing thereof, the burden of proof of a bona fide intention to acquire or to sell the shares, goods, wares or merchandise or to deliver or to receive delivery thereof, as the case may be, lies on the accused.
@ref s 383(2) (src:7221-7222)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is established that the accused made or signed a contract or an agreement for the sale or purchase of shares of stock or goods, wares or merchandise, or acted, aided or abetted in the making or signing thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 383(2) the burden of proof of a bona fide intention lies on the accused` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are under this section` AND `it is established that the accused made or signed a contract or an agreement for the sale or purchase of shares of stock or goods, wares or merchandise, or acted, aided or abetted in the making or signing thereof`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in proceedings under this section, it is established that the accused made or signed a contract or an agreement"

§§ `Section 384 -- Broker reducing stock by selling for their own account`

DECLARE `s 384(1) capacity` IS ONE OF
    `s 384(1) an individual`
    `s 384(1) a member or employee of a partnership`
    `s 384(1) a director, officer or employee of a corporation`
    `s 384(1) a person in none of those capacities`

-- (1) Every person commits an offence who, being an individual, or a member or employee of a partnership, or a director, officer or employee of a corporation, if they or the partnership or corporation is employed as a broker
-- by any customer to buy and carry on margin any shares of ... company or undertaking, ..., later sells or causes to be sold shares of the company or undertaking for any account in which they or their firm or a partner of the firm or
-- the corporation or a director of the corporation has a direct or indirect interest, if the effect of the sale is, otherwise than unintentionally, to reduce the amount of those shares ... below the amount of those shares that the broker should be carrying for all customers.
-- src:7223 | Broker reducing stock by selling for their own account
-- src:7224 | 384 (1) Every person commits an offence who, being an individual, or a member or employee of a partnership, or a director, officer or employee of a corporation, if they or the partnership or corporation is employed as a broker by any customer to buy and carry on margin any shares of an incorporated or unincorporated company or undertaking, whether in or outside Canada, later sells or causes to be sold shares of the company or undertaking for any account in which they or their firm or a partner of the firm or the corporation or a director of the corporation has a direct or indirect interest, if the effect of the sale is, otherwise than unintentionally, to reduce the amount of those shares in the hands of the broker or under their control in the ordinary course of business below the amount of those shares that the broker should be carrying for all customers.
@ref s 384(1) (src:7223-7224)
GIVEN capacity IS A `s 384(1) capacity`
      `they or the partnership or corporation is employed as a broker by a customer to buy and carry on margin any shares of a company or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person later sells or causes to be sold shares of the company or undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sale is for an account in which they or their firm or a partner of the firm or the corporation or a director of the corporation has a direct or indirect interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effect of the sale is, otherwise than unintentionally, to reduce the amount of those shares in the hands of the broker or under their control in the ordinary course of business below the amount of those shares that the broker should be carrying for all customers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 384(1) the conduct is the offence of a broker reducing stock by selling for their own account` MEANS
    IF    NOT (capacity EQUALS `s 384(1) a person in none of those capacities`)
      AND `they or the partnership or corporation is employed as a broker by a customer to buy and carry on margin any shares of a company or undertaking`
      AND `the person later sells or causes to be sold shares of the company or undertaking`
      AND `the sale is for an account in which they or their firm or a partner of the firm or the corporation or a director of the corporation has a direct or indirect interest`
      AND `the effect of the sale is, otherwise than unintentionally, to reduce the amount of those shares in the hands of the broker or under their control in the ordinary course of business below the amount of those shares that the broker should be carrying for all customers`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, being an individual, or a member or employee of a partnership, or a director, officer or employee of a corporation"

-- src:7225 | Punishment
-- src:7226 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:7227 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:7228 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 384(2) (the punishments) (src:7225-7228)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 384(2) the punishments` MEANS LIST
    (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- limb 1: the limb the text states
    , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- limb 2: the text states no penalty: s 787(1)

@ref s 384(2) (the class of the offence) (src:7225-7228)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 384(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§§ `Section 385 -- Fraudulent concealment of title documents`

DECLARE `s 385(1) capacity` IS ONE OF
    `s 385(1) a vendor, mortgagor or hypothecary debtor of property or a chose in action or an incorporeal right`
    `s 385(1) a lawyer or notary for, or an agent or mandatary of, such a vendor, mortgagor or hypothecary debtor`
    `s 385(1) a person in neither capacity`

-- src:7229 | Fraudulent concealment of title documents
-- src:7230 | 385 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who, being a vendor, mortgagor or hypothecary debtor of property or a chose in action or an incorporeal right or being a lawyer or notary for or agent or mandatary of a vendor, mortgagor or hypothecary debtor of property, a chose in action or incorporeal right, is served with a written demand for an abstract of title by or on behalf of the purchaser, mortgagee or hypothecary creditor before the completion of the purchase, mortgage or hypothec, and who
-- src:7231 | (a) with intent to defraud and for the purpose of inducing the purchaser, mortgagee or hypothecary creditor to accept the title offered or produced to them, conceals from them any settlement, deed, will or other instrument or act material to the title, or any encumbrance on the title, or
-- src:7232 | (b) falsifies any pedigree on which the title depends.
@ref s 385(1) (src:7229-7232)
GIVEN capacity IS A `s 385(1) capacity`
      `the person is served with a written demand for an abstract of title by or on behalf of the purchaser, mortgagee or hypothecary creditor before the completion of the purchase, mortgage or hypothec` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, with intent to defraud and for the purpose of inducing the purchaser, mortgagee or hypothecary creditor to accept the title offered or produced to them, conceals from them any settlement, deed, will or other instrument or act material to the title, or any encumbrance on the title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person falsifies any pedigree on which the title depends` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 385(1) the conduct is the offence of fraudulent concealment of title documents` MEANS
    IF    NOT (capacity EQUALS `s 385(1) a person in neither capacity`)
      AND `the person is served with a written demand for an abstract of title by or on behalf of the purchaser, mortgagee or hypothecary creditor before the completion of the purchase, mortgage or hypothec`
      AND (   `the person, with intent to defraud and for the purpose of inducing the purchaser, mortgagee or hypothecary creditor to accept the title offered or produced to them, conceals from them any settlement, deed, will or other instrument or act material to the title, or any encumbrance on the title`   -- (a)
           OR `the person falsifies any pedigree on which the title depends`)   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who, being a vendor, mortgagor or hypothecary debtor of property"

@ref s 385(1) (the punishments) (src:7229-7232)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
